WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.734
-I always love when you come on.
Thank you so much for coming

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:03.934
back to the show, bud.
-They just told me

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:05.434
I've been here nine times.
-Isn't that crazy?

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:06.634
-That's crazy right there.
-I want you to be here

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:07.667
100 times.
-Let's go.

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.100
-I can't get enough of you, bud.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.400
I have something here that I
don't think I've ever thought

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.834
I'd see in my lifetime,

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:15.133
and I've been a fan of yours
for a long time.

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:18.067
You are on a Cheerios box.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.601
Look at that.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:25.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I made it!

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.334
-Wow, Honey Nut Cheerios.

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.234
If you ever told me
as a kid like,

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.467
"Ice-T is going to be
on a cereal box --"

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.667
-Impossible.
You could put a gun to my head

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:34.801
and said -- I'd be like, "No.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.067
No way is that going to
ever happen."

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:37.767
And I'd be shot
because it happened.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.467
-Are you a fan or did they reach
out? How did it happen?

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:43.868
-They reached out,
you know what I'm saying?

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.400
I'm a little older now,
and they wanted

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.501
somebody to represent
heart health.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:50.901
And, you know, it's been
a changing of the guards, Jimmy.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.701
You know, the people
that were scared of us

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.434
in hip-hop are gone now.

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:56.601
So you go to the CEOs
of these big companies,

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:59.334
they're like 45-year-old guys,
you know, or women,

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:00.701
and they're just like,
"I love you."

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.701
I mean, that's how we made it
into the Super Bowl.

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.501
You know, everybody
who was at the Super Bowl

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.234
were the "bad guys," you know?

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:09.033
50 and em all of --
Snoop and everybody.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:12.334
So the guards have changed,
and now the people in power

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:14.968
love hip-hop,
and I'm on a Cheerios box.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:20.467
-I think it's great.
Isn't that wild?

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:22.767
That's so good.
I think It's an honor.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.868
It actually also inspired

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:27.167
something
called the Ice-T challenge.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.968
This is a thing
that you did not start.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.701
Your fans started this.
-They started it.

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:32.334
What they would do is
they'd go in the stores

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:35.000
and they'd flip the box around
to where they said,

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.901
"Ice, you should have been
on the front of the box."

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:41.167
And all over the country, people
are flipping these boxes around.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.501
It's real crazy.
-Look at this.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.634
This is actually happening
in grocery stores.

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:46.767
People just going in,
they go, "No."

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:50.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:53.601
I like that challenge.
-It's cool, it's cool.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.000
You know, it's fun.
Nobody gets hurt.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.067
-I'm going to do it
this weekend.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.834
-Yeah.
-I think it's fun.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:01.200
I think it's good.
I'll get the kids doing it too.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.634
You know, I follow you
on the socials.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:04.167
You're a great follow.
I've said this before.

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.834
I do love following you.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.300
But this thing caught my eye the
other day, and I was concerned.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.767
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:11.300
And it got national attention.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.701
This is from you, @finallevel.

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.267
It says,
"I was robbed at a gas station

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.033
in New Jersey last night.

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.767
After my hand stopped trembling,
I managed to call the cops.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.567
They were quick to respond
and calm me down.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:23.734
My money is gone.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.133
The police asked me
if I knew who did it,

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.367
and I said,
'Yes. It was pump number nine.'"

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:33.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:40.734
That's a good joke.

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:43.734
-That joke got a million likes.

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:47.100
I never got a million likes on
Twitter before.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.968
I got to tell the truth.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.734
My buddy Caz,
from Rollin' Sixties

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:54.100
hit me with that joke,
and I kind of rewrote it

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.467
and I put I was in New Jersey
and all that kind of stuff.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:58.501
So, I kind of plagiarized
his joke.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:02:59.534
He gets some credit, too.

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:00.734
-Yeah, Caz, yeah,
you get a little --

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.701
-Yeah, Caz hooked it up.
-Yeah, he hooked up.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:03.834
-But it was on the news.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:06.400
I'm watching,
you know, channel -- CNN.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.734
"Ice-T gets robbed."
People like negative stuff.

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:12.133
I think what caught everyone's
attention was the fact,

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.534
"Ooh, something bad happened."

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.767
You know, people like stuff
that happens bad to people.

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:18.334
If it said Ice-T won something,
that something great happened,

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:19.534
they'd scroll right by.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:20.934
"He got robbed! What happened?"

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.367
You know what I'm saying?
And then I got them in the end

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:25.367
with pump nine,
you know I'm saying?

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:27.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
-You got them with the joke.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.100
Pump nine -- I loved it.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.200
You also do a thing,
a recurring thing on Twitter,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.434
a thing called Ice Cold Facts.
-Yeah.

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:40.701
-And these are inspirational
sometimes, motivational tweets

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.300
from you, pieces of advice
from you.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.501
-Things I've heard or things I
made up, just things that people

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.667
need to know
that are actually facts.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:50.000
-I thought that we could go
through a few of your tweets

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.100
and you can tell us
a little more about

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.167
your thoughts behind them.
-Let's go.

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.434
-Okay.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:58.534
I like that.
That's pretty good too.

00:03:58.534 --> 00:04:00.667
"Let's go" is even good.
-That's a fact.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.701
We're about to go.
-Let's go.

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:04.501
We're about to go. That's right.

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:06.200
Alright, ice cold fact.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.067
"At some point you're going to
realize that

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:11.400
if you don't go get it,
it's not going to get got."

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:16.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.734
-That is --

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.067
Dude, that's good.

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:23.334
-I mean, you just can't sit on
the -- You can't say,

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:25.434
"I'm gonna go to gym"
and just sit on the couch.

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:26.734
It's not like you're
just automatically

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:28.968
going to get in shape.
You've got to go.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:33.067
And anything you want, no one --
I'll back that up with no one

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:35.601
wakes up in the morning
with your dream.

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.901
Whatever your dream is,
it's yours.

00:04:37.901 --> 00:04:39.267
So if you want it to happen,

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:41.267
you have to make it happen
personally.

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:43.667
Don't expect it to happen
because someone else

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:45.601
is going to care about
what you want.

00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:48.667
-Yeah. I love that.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:50.267
I love that.

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.601
Ice cold fact.
-Uh-oh.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.567
-"A lie will get around
the world twice

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.434
before the truth can get
its pants on."

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:01.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.033
-Kind of going back to
what I'm saying.

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:05.167
People love the lies,
they love the drama,

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:08.534
so drama spreads really,
really fast, you know?

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:12.033
Something that's true
and positive, unfortunately,

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:14.100
humans don't connect to that.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.968
I mean, that's just a case study
in our human nature.

00:05:16.968 --> 00:05:19.000
-Yeah. And then -- Yeah.
But I like it can go

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.934
around the world before
the truth can get its pants on.

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:22.601
-Yeah, before you can even get
up. What they lying about?

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:23.968
-Yeah, what's that about?
-What they lying about?

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:26.567
Let me tell them. It's too late.

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:27.667
-I'll do this last one.

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:29.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:32.334
I want to do this last one.
Ice cold fact.

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:34.133
"If you follow me on
Twitter or Instagram,

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.667
your life will improve."

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:40.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:43.200
I agree.
I totally agree as a follower.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.801
I love seeing your stuff.

00:05:44.801 --> 00:05:47.167
It always makes me laugh
and it always makes me think.

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:48.667
-I mean, there's nothing to be
said about that.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:50.300
That's just an ice cold fact.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.467
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:54.434
I want to talk about
"Law &amp; Order: SVU."

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:55.434
-Let's go.

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:56.968
-You're about to wrap up
season 23.

00:05:56.968 --> 00:05:58.200
Is that possible?

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.467
-Right now, we are filming

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:02.167
the final episode of season 23.

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.901
We got the record at 21,

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:07.834
and now I'm hoping we go to
like season 29 or something.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:12.100
I mean, this year we had some
of the best ratings ever.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.033
It's just -- I'm lucky to be
on board that ship.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:18.701
-Can you tell us
how the season ends?

00:06:18.701 --> 00:06:20.400
-I don't die.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.133
-Okay, alright,
well, that's good.

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:23.534
Do you worry about that?

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:25.834
-Yeah.

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:29.100
Yeah, when you're on a show
this long, like, you know,

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.434
I read the script and I get
shot, I'm like, "I'm shot."

00:06:31.434 --> 00:06:34.100
And I start "uh, uh, uh, uh,
oh, oh, oh, right there."

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.634
[ Both exhale ]
"I'm alive."

00:06:35.634 --> 00:06:37.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.400
I got shot on page 20.
43, I'm breathing.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.400
[ Laughter ]
Yes!

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.267
-"I love you, Dick Wolf."

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:46.968
-I'm like, "Yo, let me know
something, man."

00:06:46.968 --> 00:06:48.434
-Congrats on another
great season.

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:49.501
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:51.734
Here's Ice-T in
"Law &amp; Order: SVU."

00:06:51.734 --> 00:06:52.834
Take a look at this.

00:06:52.834 --> 00:06:54.067
-It'll be worth it.

00:06:54.067 --> 00:06:56.267
Juana Ramirez is the soul
of this neighborhood.

00:06:56.267 --> 00:06:58.067
-If anything is going on,
she'll know about it.

00:06:58.067 --> 00:06:59.400
-Okay, I'm gonna wait out here.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:02.601
Nobody likes a bakery
full of cops.

00:07:02.601 --> 00:07:05.801
Get me a coffee and some chisme.

00:07:05.801 --> 00:07:08.634
-Come on, Ice-T, everybody.
Come on, you know how to do it.

